gpui_macos: accept drags of text, HTML, RTF, URLs and image data

Registers the window for plain text, HTML, RTF/RTFD, URL and common image
types next to file names. A drag without file names is announced as
`FileDropEvent::DataEntered` with the pasteboard's types; at the drop the
accepted flavors are read and handed over as `DataSubmit`: every accepted
text type, small metadata (a link's title, the source page, an editor's
language hint) and only the first offered image type. Private and dynamic
types, file promises and further image representations are never read.
Each representation has a byte limit (text 32 MiB, image 64 MiB, metadata
64 KiB) and all reads together 128 MiB; a representation over its limit is
skipped and released at once. File drags are unchanged. Depends on the
gpui change that adds `ExternalData`.

